cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SENTINEL: an authority-attenuating immune architecture for AI agents"
message: "If you use this prototype or its results, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Milan
    given-names: Jerson Boyd
    alias: jersonboydmilan
    website: "https://github.com/jersonboydmilan"
repository-code: "https://github.com/jersonboydmilan/sentinel"
abstract: >-
  A research prototype investigating whether an ecosystem of autonomous AI
  agents can detect and contain compromised agents without transferring
  unrestricted authority to the agents responsible for defence. Contributions:
  behavioural agent identity, authority drift, agent immune memory, defensive
  authority, and recursive governance, evaluated with deterministic simulations,
  adversarial suites and an out-of-process verification split.
keywords:
  - AI agent security
  - capability-based security
  - authority drift
  - multi-agent systems
  - AI safety
license: MIT
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-09-20"
